Package: HazardMaps
Type: Package
Title: Spatial Dependence Modeling and Pseudoscenario Generation for Natural Hazards
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Maria Valentina", "Clavijo Mesa",
                   email = "valentina.clavijo@usp.br",
                   role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An R package for reproducible analysis of spatial dependence in environmental
             and climate-related variables. The package provides a unified workflow to
             ingest spatial datasets, estimate and visualize spatial correlation structures,
             fit multiple dependence models including vine copulas (C-vine and D-vine),
             Gaussian models, and stochastic fields, and compare them using quantitative
             indicators to support model selection. Based on the selected model, the package
             enables the generation of spatially dependent pseudoscenarios for uncertainty
             analysis and simulation studies. The design emphasizes numerical robustness,
             modularity, and reproducibility across heterogeneous spatial data sources.
